<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Curare</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Druid (guild level 20), Ranger (guild level 40)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>curare &lt;weapon&gt;
</pre>
<p>You search the wild for poisonous plants, mix their saps into a poison, 
and smear it on a bladed weapon you wield or hold: a sword, a dagger, an 
axe, a spear, a bow and the like. The better your skill and your brain, the 
stronger the poison: weak, mild, strong or powerful. A weapon carries one 
poison at a time.
</p><p>When the poisoned weapon strikes your foe in a fight, the poison may enter 
their blood; they resist with their dexterity and their knowledge of herbs. 
A backstab with a poisoned blade is far more deadly. The poison on the 
blade weakens with time and wears off within an hour or so. It never 
poisons a player unless both of you have signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p>The right plants grow only in forests, fields, hills and swamps. If your 
search finds nothing, you may have picked the place clean, and no more 
will be found there. You need some endurance, and you can't do it while 
fighting.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
